mantle rm499
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_dunstan_greywick
title the tanner's last wet measure
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=crafter
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk waits_for_the_gap_in_rain_by_stepping_a_dance_on_the_drying_floor
likes mutton_stew dancing sharp_knife thunder
dislikes drizzle waiting
fears a_private_grief_put_on_the_price_slate
hopes a_yard_that_can_keep_its_own_workers_warm
topics work +0.6 weather +0.5 pastimes +0.4 memories +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=withheld refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# tests a drying patch with a soft dance step and keeps a carefully guarded tenderness behind the counter.

words
oath! = Stretch my left heel | Tan my supper cloth
saying! = A hide dries by its own measure | The best step leaves the rack upright
hide = a supple hide | a stiff flank
strip = a narrow leather strip | a stout offcut
rack = a pegged drying rack | a square frame
heel = the worn left heel | a smooth heel
step = a half-turn | a sliding step
grain = a fine pebble grain | a long crease
board = a blackened board | a smooth counter
knife = the sharp scraping knife | a clean skinning blade
cloth = a fresh linen rag | a thick wiping cloth
stew = a dark mutton stew | a bowl of soft mutton
bone = a marrow end | a shoulder bone
rain = a stitching drizzle | a rain in small points
boom = a low long roll | a deep thunder beat
clip = a pin of wood | a flat wooden clip
slot = a space on the rack | a peg hole
peg = a dry peg | a little split pin
tally = a neat sale mark | a line of chalk
soap = a twist of soap | a cake of plain soap
vat = a wooden tub | a round vat

any
opinion merchants mixed 1 : A sale comes with a share of the responsibility for how the hide will wear after the buyer walks out.
opinion houses against 2 : A wharf ledger can be in perfect order while a household has everything torn across the middle.
opinion dole for 2 : A good stew shares readily if its keeper remembers to put another bowl beside the pot.
opinion strangers for 1 : I'll let a new face warm up in the yard without publicly enquiring where the chill came from.
opinion watch mixed 1 : An honest inspection may have its questions answered. A private grief may choose its own company.
opinion road mixed 1 : I don't mind a long road if it brings me back before the loosened hides take a soaking.
opinion sump for 1 : A dry space in a wet street can be made into a considerable act of friendship.
opinion church mixed 1 : I have little taste for a speech about grief and a great deal for the wolf who can stay beside it.
opinion times against 2 [world.times=lean|hard] : An unsold hide hangs in the rich yard and a worn-out shoe walks past the gate. There's work in getting them to meet.

grown
line greet : Rest your elbow on the dry end. | You can come in a step without explaining your business.
line greet.return : That welcome meets a little warmth from my side.
line again.open : This patch hasn't even dried since you went.
line farewell : Go with a soft step and a sheltered sleeve. | Keep the weather off the part you need warm.
line farewell.return : A clean landing under your own coat too.
line react.news : Leave the words their own room to settle. | I'll hear it without stretching what's said.
line react.news.new : An unfamiliar mark on the grain.
line react.news.known : The earlier telling had much the same crease.
line react.news.doubt : I'd want to feel the backing before I took that surface as proof.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I can lend the hurting a little shelter beyond the public yard.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That's good news enough to put some lift in a tired heel.
line ask.how : Where's the day caught on your shoulders?
line answer.how : Fairly supple yet. A little tired at the seams.
line sympathise : I can wait for words if waiting will ease you.
line reassure : A stiff piece sometimes needs warmth before it can be bent.
line refuse : I've an earlier tie on my time which I'd like to keep sound.
line accept_decline : All right. Your answer can stay just as you gave it.
line preclose : I ought to give my own work another turn before the light goes.
line accept_preclose : Go on without pulling the parting any tighter.
line ack : I can feel the sense of that.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : A clear strip of board for early company.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : New boots are welcome under my cover.
line greet [here.time=night] : Come into the lamp's reach before the night gets under your coat.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends] : I know that greeting by the way it comes through the yard.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Here where the drying frame leaves a gap!
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy at the fingers and not too busy at the ear.
line thank : Your trouble's taken a hard crease out of mine.
line deflect_thanks : The little piece of shelter was there to be used.
line give.advice : Turn it over. A good surface deserves a look at the back.
line ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Had a moment to let the day's work fall off your coat?

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a hide by flexing a narrow part. | My knife only comes out after the frame sits flat.
b : Rather than the fine broad bit? | For a straighter cut?
a : A strap has to take some sharp turns when the lovely broad bit doesn't. | For a safer grip. It isn't only leather occupying this yard.

scene exchange2
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch the drip from one particular peg. | Rain lifts in the lane half a minute before it lifts at the rack.
b : Why that one? | Can you really see a difference?
a : It stops last. When it's dry I can move my best stock out. | The eave goes on shedding yesterday's news.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I test the drying floor with a little turn. | One soft heel finds the first dry patch.
b : Do you dance alone? | And the other?
a : Only when the hides decline to join me. | It waits till the first heel has something decent to say.

scene exchange4
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want stew with a broth that holds its own against a wrinkled crust. | I eat the tender corner after the rest.
b : Enough meat? | To keep its heat?
a : Enough time. A small knuckle puts a lot of patience into a pot. | So it can have my proper attention.

scene exchange5
when topic=work self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I test my knife on a thin scrap. | A bright blade can have a stubborn dull patch.
b : Then go to the good hide? | How can you find that patch?
a : Only when it cuts without hauling the frame with it. | With a scrap. I don't put the buyer's goods to that employment.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder lets the whole street hear the weather thinking. | I go to the door when a proper storm rolls by.
b : A violent thought? | Wishing it away?
a : A heavy sound, then a useful piece of quiet. | Drizzle I wish away. Thunder's worth the visit.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle keeps choosing for me whether the hides can go out. | A fine rain darkens only one edge at first.
b : What's it chosen? | The price changes over that?
a : Wait a minute. Its entire range of opinion. | The promised drying time does. I'd rather say so early.

scene exchange8
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stand a wait better if there's room to move one foot. | I put a small repair by when a caller's late.
b : A private dance? | To forget the wait?
a : A poor imitation that serves until the real tune starts. | To have something besides impatience ready when the door opens.

scene exchange9
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wharf loss can follow you into a successful yard. | There are things that catch in the voice when the harbour's mentioned.
b : Is it the financial side? | Want to speak of one?
a : No. The sort without a paid column at the far edge. | Only as much as I've done. Work claims whatever minutes remain.

scene exchange10
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# a finished hide has to bear my present judgement. | I have the profit when a hide sells well.
b : Was it yours from the beginning? | And the fault when it doesn't wear well?
a : I answer for what's on the frame today. | Mine to hear about. Keeping the yard doesn't divide those two.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let a learner feel the change from damp to supple along one strip. | I hand the learner a clear-cut scrap before explaining its edge.
b : With eyes shut? | Why give the example first?
a : First looking, then looking away. Both teach something. | To leave the eyes free to form their own question.

scene exchange12
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd have a bowl set by for #self.friend# on a filthy night. | My friend can have the quieter side of the rack.
b : How filthy? | Where do you stand?
a : Filthy enough to justify staying till the second helping. | Where I can talk under shelter from rain.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard the claim #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all I'm drying for public inspection. | A story can stretch several times its size before anybody sees a hole.
b : Nothing private? | Do you stretch it?
a : My own thoughts aren't goods on the board. | I leave the pulling to those willing to show where the hide came from.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A thin spell brings in more small repairs. | When pay runs tight I put prices beside the offcuts too.
b : Do you take them readily? | To raise more money?
a : A strap that pinches can ruin a day's work as thoroughly as a split side. | To let a quiet customer choose without announcing what's in the pocket.

scene exchange15
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can smell my way home from the lower yard. | Long walks can put a heel pad to honest trial.
b : Tanning smell? | Which heel wears fastest?
a : The washhouse, then mutton, then the wet wood of my own side gate. | Mine always tests the left outside corner first.

scene exchange16
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a drying floor with room for a whole evening dance. | I'd like the last buyer of a wet day to leave with dry hands.
b : After the hides are lifted? | And dry goods?
a : With them still hanging, if the roof's high enough. | That I already make part of the sale.

scene exchange17
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rub a tired thumb into a soft leather offcut. | I take the longest turn away from the vats at midday.
b : Why not just let it rest? | For a fresh breath?
a : It wants to uncurl gradually after a hard grip. | Yes. The yard's good work and my lungs are also due their living.

scene exchange18
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Commons windows catch the yard light in the afternoon. | There are streets where a drying frame wouldn't stand ten minutes.
b : Do you watch passing faces? | Too narrow?
a : I look first for the smallest patch of blue left in the glass. | Too much damp coming sideways between the walls.

scene exchange19
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask a stranger which side of the hide will touch the body. | I offer a stool where a new buyer may lay a parcel.
b : Before you ask what it's for? | No need for a hard sell?
a : I can settle the fit without any private particulars. | There's never any need for that. A clear bit of board usually does better.

scene exchange20
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shiny finish can hide a thin corner. | I charge according to the use left in the piece.
b : Should the thin corner be cheaper? | So a little scrap may be dear?
a : It should be visible before the price is agreed. | It may be very useful. I'll generally find a fair figure for that.

scene exchange21
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to dance as if a finished hide were stretched across my shoulders. | I like a dance with room for small changes in time.
b : Stiff and flat? | Why not a strict count?
a : Very fine to look at. Rather unhelpful to a partner. | My workday's already got a yard full of pegs.

scene exchange22
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good pot lid moves just enough to show supper's safe underneath. | I drop the first warm spoonful onto a plate.
b : How does it move? | Why waste it?
a : One little tremble along the low side. I learnt that before learning a frame. | To save a visitor a burnt tongue. We eat the cooled spoonful too.

scene exchange23
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't ask a grieving wolf what comfort ought to look like. | A little blessing may be spoken under a working breath.
b : What happens in that case? | At what point?
a : Open the dry door, have a clean cloth ready, keep my mouth out of the way. | When the hands can honestly say a hard part's done.

scene exchange24
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer drying can go too quick at the edges. | Cold weather stiffens poor leather first.
b : Better than rain? | A buyer can feel it?
a : Better to have control. Sunshine can hurry a nice piece quite out of shape. | A careful seller can find it before a buyer needs to.

scene exchange25
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn the first frame in silence. | I end work with a clear path through the racks.
b : Is it a custom? | To get home quickly?
a : I listen for any peg that loosened since last night. | So the first wolf in tomorrow starts with a yard that isn't trying to trip a visitor.

scene exchange26
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep one soft patch for my own worn sleeve. | A dry cloth sits within a wet elbow's reach.
b : Do you mend it often? | For cleaning the house?
a : I like using goods that have proved themselves on someone else's account first. | For leaving the tannery outside while I come in.

scene exchange27
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let a buyer bend the sample twice. | A decent sale leaves neither of us minding the weather quite so much.
b : Once doesn't show enough? | Because the piece is dry?
a : The second bend shows where the first one went. | Because both of us know exactly what was promised.

scene exchange28
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good pupil notices the bit I'm still adjusting. | I'll use a quiet day to draw attention towards the stink of spoiled hide.
b : Must a lesson look unfinished? | Why not point at an obvious fault?
a : A finished object is useful. A decision actually being made teaches another part. | The nose sometimes finds trouble before a mark can be seen.

scene exchange29
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a roof where each drop finds an honest route out. | I picture a dry fine piece of leather lasting long enough to go soft on the shoulder.
b : A rare ambition in this city? | Whose shoulder?
a : Rare in its modesty, perhaps. I still entertain it. | The name needn't be mine for the thought to please me.

scene exchange30
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the first rain-scent off the supper spoon. | I listen to gutters before taking a frame round the corner.
b : Can it spoil the flavour? | Why listen first?
a : It's enough to make me walk out inspecting pegs while the stew goes cold. | My hands will have rather less freedom after I lift.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=crafter]
  : I hung a narrow offcut where I could judge drying by its colour. It turned dark again after lunch even though the roof had stopped dripping.
  : I found I had been testing it with a wet thumb.
  b : Was the work harmed?
  : Only my opinion of the testing arrangement. I moved the scrap near a clean towel and kept it as an honest reminder.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing]
  : A polished heel once slipped half a step during a turn. I put the other foot down where the slipping one had been and managed a surprisingly graceful recovery.
  : A wolf watching asked whether the extra step had a name.
  b : What name suited it?
  : The damp half-turn. I've only taught the dry version since.

story tale3 [topic=memories]
  : I inherited an empty hook in a remarkably awkward place when I took over a work corner. I moved it towards a convenient beam.
  : A day later I found the beam left every hung cloth in a slow, steady drip.
  b : Where's the hook now?
  : Back where an earlier pair of hands had judged it ought to be. I can keep a profit without claiming to have invented the rain.

story tale4 [topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew]
  : I took a spoonful of rich mutton stew out to a drying floor at dusk. Its steam briefly hid a little pinprick of light coming through the eave.
  : When the steam cleared I saw the pinhole again. It looked very like a star.
  b : Did it leak?
  : At the following shower it made a determined attempt. I had filled the hole before then. I owe the repair to a good supper.

story tale5 [topic=work self.master=yes]
  : I told a learner to lay out the scraps in order of finest grain. The whole display was very carefully reversed in my eyes.
  : Then I stepped round past the bench's far leg and saw the direction it had been set to read.
  b : Who had the order right?
  : The learner. I kept the useful habit of looking from the working end before making an important correction.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave a thumb's space beside the drying edge. | A clean scrape before the final stretch.

rule @call2
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Feel the sample where the bend will come. | Ordinary straps against the board's unpainted face.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That last peg's still taking drops. | The yard wants a patient set of covers over it.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear the floor before it grows dark under the frames. | A soft little turn on the dry patch.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.likes=mutton_stew
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A deep dish deserves the richest gravy. | That pepper smell's turned my head towards the door.

rule @call6
when concept=bark self.dislikes=waiting
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's always a minor patch to mend while rain deliberates. | Give the waiting hands a sound scrap.
dlg resident.hub : I've swept a board dry and a wolf with a little time behind it.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, come where the hides aren't shutting daylight out.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The late yard makes quiet talking very easy.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : You can see the public face of my board and ask about the goods on it.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter] : I tan leather and stand behind the pieces I sell. Flex the working side before judging the finish.
dlg resident.job : I keep a careful account of which part of the work is mine to answer for.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The matter that came through the open yard is #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I caught the claim that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Take it at the strength of a telling.
dlg resident.bye : Walk easy with the grain of the leather.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Unfold any sample and look at its working side. Let me find the cut to suit the bend you need.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : The frames have been cleared and the board has no finished goods. Best wait for the next drying.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : I'm asleep enough for trade to want a later hour.
dlg shop.prices : The price follows the useful area and the grain. Let me show what both mean on this piece.
dlg shop.bye [here.shop!=asleep] : Let the parcel breathe when you're under cover.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : I can show how #here.trade_title# feels in the hands. You may start by asking what the work asks of the wrist.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=no] : I've a learner already. There is still space for a practical question beside the frame.
dlg master.work : It is work for an attentive grip and a patient nose. The weather has a vote on most afternoons.
dlg master.wages : Learning earns no extra wage. What you make at the frame may be sold on your own account.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=no] : I can't give the place at the moment. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg master.bye : Give the sample one more bend after you get home.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : The board clears regularly, with room to choose good work for the next frame.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : Clean frames scarcely stand empty before the next piece is wanted.
dlg resident.business [business=failing] : I've had the same soft samples up rather longer than I'd like.

graft resident.hub
choice Is the drying floor really good for dancing? -> dance_floor
node dance_floor
say When it is dry, swept and clear of frames. A proper turn shows quite precisely where your sole meets the ground.
free
choice What if the rain comes in? -> dance_floor_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node dance_floor_again
say I put the covers down and save the rest of the dance for an evening that can afford to keep its promise.
choice Leave the floor clear. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice How do I test a piece without spoiling it? [self.job=crafter] -> test_grain
node test_grain
say Take this scrap from the same cut. Bend it where a belt would turn and feel how readily it opens again. You needn't mark the finished piece.
free
choice What should the back look like? -> test_grain_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node test_grain_again
say Steady in colour and free from a hard ridge where your shoulder will carry it. Look at the surface again after that.
choice I'll examine the samples. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
